camchrome: an Android persona has overlay scrollbars.

Android Chrome draws overlay scrollbars that take no layout width. On a Linux or Windows host the
renderer kept the host's classic 15 px scrollbar, so an Android persona reported
innerWidth - clientWidth = 15 on any scrolling page, and every overflow:scroll box lost 15 px: a
desktop scrollbar under a phone UA. The renderer now enables overlay scrollbars (and turns Fluent
scrollbars off) when the persona is Android, as DevTools' mobile emulation does.

The renderer-side switch alone did not hold: the browser sends use_overlay_scrollbar in the
renderer preferences from the host's NativeTheme, and WebViewImpl applies it after start-up. The
browser now derives that preference from the persona too (web_contents_impl.cc): Android gets
overlay scrollbars, Windows and Linux personas classic ones (also on a Mac host with overlay
scrollbars, which reported 0 px), and a macOS persona keeps the host style.

Checked by fingerprint_selftest's scrollbar-width-matches-persona-os with --platform.

